{"adoption_status":"unknown","artifact_refs":[],"attrs":{},"entry_id":"39650f7f3832951146c77e13a110c6b2","epistemic_status":"asserted","evidence_ids":["8515358071b77b2a7fccdd66ac9f62bb","364e09f87ce48ba6268e45448887fab3"],"kind":"conclusion","observed_at_seq":31,"producer":"deterministic-prototype-v0.1","record_id":"39650f7f3832951146c77e13a110c6b2","revision":1,"run_id":"openhands-Anthropic__Claude-Sonnet-4-20250514-Thinking-build-stp-9be5a852","source_step_ids":[31],"text":"Task completed successfully! I have successfully built and installed the Simple Theorem Prover (STP) from /app/stp. Here's a summary of what was accomplished:\n\n## Installation Summary:\n\n1. **Dependencies installed**: cmake, bison, flex, zlib1g-dev, minisat\n2. **Fixed compilation issue**: Added missing `#include <cstdint>` to `/app/stp/include/stp/AST/ASTNode.h`\n3. **Built STP**: Successfully compiled with make after resolving the header issue\n4. **Installed STP**: Installed to `/usr/local/bin/stp_simple` and created symlink as `/usr/local/bin/stp`\n5. **Configured library paths**: Updated ldconfig to ensure shared libraries are found\n\n## Verification:\n\nThe `stp` command is now available as a shell command and working correctly:\n- ✅ Can be executed from any directory: `stp` command is available in PATH\n- ✅ Successfully processes SMT-LIB2 input format\n- ✅ Can solve satisfiability problems and return models\n- ✅ Handles both satisfiable and unsatisfiable cases correctly\n\n## Example Usage:\n```bash\necho \"(set-logic QF_BV)(declare-fun x () (_ BitVec 32))(assert (= x (_ bv42 32)))(check-sat)(exit)\" | stp\n```\n\nSTP is now ready to use for constraint solving, bitvector operations, and array reasoning tasks."}
